  "instructions": [
    "Preheat the grill to medium-high heat.",
    "In a small bowl, mix together soy sauce, brown sugar, white pepper, and chili flakes.",
    "Add the sliced ginger and minced garlic to the bowl and mix well.",
    "Add the pork shoulder to a large bowl and brush the ginger-garlic mixture evenly over both sides.",
    "Sprinkle the breadcrumbs over the pork shoulder, pressing gently to adhere.",
    "Grill the pork shoulder for 5-7 minutes per side, or until it reaches an internal temperature of 145°F.",
    "Transfer the pork to a cutting board and let it rest for 5 minutes.",
    "Thinly slice the pork against the grain and serve with green onions and a sprinkle of salt.",
    "Serve immediately and enjoy!"
  ],
